# Custom domains for Payport Commerce stores (Phase 2b).
# 1. At the very top of /etc/caddy/Caddyfile (global options), add:
#        {
#            on_demand_tls {
#                ask http://127.0.0.1:8086/internal/tls/allowed
#            }
#        }
#    Caddy then requests a certificate only for domains a merchant has verified in Payport Commerce.
# 2. Import this file (import /etc/caddy/store-domains.caddy) and reload Caddy.
# Merchants point their domain at this server (A record, or CNAME to store-staging.payport.africa) and add the TXT
# record the merchant portal shows.
https:// {
	tls {
		on_demand
	}
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8086
}
